<%- include('partials/head', { pageClass: 'page-legal' }) %>

<article class="legal">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: 30 August 2026</p>

  <p>
    <%= SITE_NAME %> is a static reference site. It has no user accounts and does
    not ask you for any personal information. This page explains what that means
    in practice, and what will change when advertising is switched on.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect today</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Nothing that identifies you.</strong> There are no sign-ups, no
      logins, no forms, and no analytics or tracking scripts at the time of
      writing.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A theme preference</strong> (light / dark / system) is stored in
      your browser&rsquo;s <code>localStorage</code>. It never leaves your device
      and is not sent to us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Standard server logs.</strong> Like almost any website, the server
      may briefly record request data such as your IP address, the page
      requested, and your browser&rsquo;s user-agent string. These are used only
      for security and debugging and are not used to build a profile of you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Offline caching.</strong> If you add the site to your home screen or
      revisit pages, a service worker stores copies of pages and assets in your
      browser cache so they load without a connection. This data stays on your
      device; you can clear it any time from your browser settings.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    The site itself currently sets <strong>no cookies</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising (planned)</h2>
  <p>
    <%= SITE_NAME %> intends to display ads through <strong>Google AdSense</strong>
    to cover hosting costs. Once ads are live:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Google and its partners may use <strong>cookies and similar technologies</strong>
      to serve and measure ads, including ads based on your prior visits to this
      site and other websites.
    </li>
    <li>
      This introduces <strong>third-party, cookie-based tracking</strong> that
      does not exist today. That data is collected and controlled by Google, not
      by <%= SITE_NAME %>.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can review and control how Google personalises ads at
      <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener">myadcenter.google.com</a>,
      and opt out of personalised advertising from many providers at
      <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info/" rel="noopener">optout.aboutads.info</a>
      or <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="noopener">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      More detail is in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">Google&rsquo;s &ldquo;How Google uses information from sites that use our services&rdquo;</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This policy will be updated with the concrete details (and any consent
    mechanism required in your region) when advertising actually goes live.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    None at present. If a privacy-respecting analytics tool is added later, this
    page will be updated to say what it collects.
  </p>

  <h2>Data sources</h2>
  <p>
    The kanji data shown on the site comes from public, freely-licensed datasets
    (listed on the <a href="/credits">credits</a> page). No information about you
    is sent to those projects or to any other third party, other than the
    advertising described above.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect
    information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may change as the site evolves — most importantly when ads are
    enabled. The &ldquo;last updated&rdquo; date above reflects the current
    version.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:<%= CONTACT_EMAIL %>"><%= CONTACT_EMAIL %></a>.
  </p>
</article>

<%- include('partials/foot', { pageClass: 'page-legal' }) %>
